Layout fixes found on XenForo forums (a1k.org), all general, none AMIX
specific; meant for upstream NetSurf as well.

 - layout.c: table-layout: fixed (CSS 2.1 17.5.2.1), which NetSurf parsed but
   never used.  For a table of a set width the first row's cells give the
   column widths (border box), the open columns share the rest equally, the
   content never widens a column; layout_minmax_table reports the first
   row's set lengths as the table's width, not its content.  XenForo lays
   out every forum row and the page with its sidebar as such tables; with
   the auto layout a one-line (nowrap) title widened its column and the
   page.
 - layout.c: a table with box-sizing: border-box takes its padding out of
   its specified width, as blocks do (it was added on top).
 - layout.c: an inline-flex box in a line is placed and gives the line its
   height as an inline-block does (it was left out: a line holding only an
   inline-flex button had height 0).
 - box_construct.c: generated content.  ::before/::after made only an empty
   block (the clearfix hack); now strings, attr() and quotes give text and
   url() an image, in blocks, inline blocks, table cells and flex
   containers, and in inline elements (after the element's box, before its
   INLINE_END).  Characters of the Unicode private use areas are left out:
   they are icon font glyphs that need the page's web font.  Counters are
   not done.
 - box_construct.c: a form control with no content of its own (text field,
   check box...) with display: flex is laid out as a block, as browsers do;
   and a flex container's child stays a blockified flex item after the
   special element conversion (box_input_text set inline-block again, so
   the field was wrapped in an anonymous block and lost its width: 100%).

